```
 
**Why exclude `data/`?** Your local SQLite database should not be copied into the image. The application should create or use its database through its configured runtime path and a persistent Docker volume where appropriate.

The `.dockerignore` rules reduce unnecessary build-context files and help prevent accidental inclusion of local secrets. <Cite refs={["turn415134search0"]}/>

# 3. Other files worth adding

<box border radius="lg" padding={3} gap={3}>
  **`.env.example`**

  A template showing which environment variables the application supports. It is safe to commit when it contains placeholders rather than real credentials.

  <CodeBlock language="bash" editable>
DATABASE_PATH=data/receipts.db
  